<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch11-triple-higher-integrals" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Triple and Higher-Dimensional Integrals</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Triple integrals extend the slicing and summation methods of Chapter 10 to solids. Cylindrical and spherical coordinates from Chapter 4 organize familiar regions, and their volume factors account for the sizes of small coordinate boxes. An optional section extends the same ideas to higher dimensions.</p>
  </introduction>

